ons [Data: Entities (7139, 1912, 2421)].\n\n## Nutritional assessments as a key component of care\n\nNutritional assessments are essential for evaluating the dietary needs of patients, particularly those at risk of malnutrition. Tools such as the Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool and the Mini Nutritional Assessment are employed to identify patients who require nutritional interventions. These assessments ensure that care plans are tailored to meet the specific needs of each patient, promoting recovery and overall health [Data: Relationships (2384, 2321)].\"\r\n\n\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n2372,ELECTROLYTES,\"Electrolytes are essential minerals in the body that carry an electric charge and play a crucial role in maintaining fluid balance and supporting various physiological functions. They are vital for hydration, muscle function, and overall bodily operations. Electrolytes, such as sodium and potassium, are particularly important and need to be monitored in patients receiving nutritional support, including those with diabetes, as their levels can vary based on health status. These minerals are often added to nutritional solutions to ensure that individuals maintain proper electrolyte levels for optimal health.\",5\r\n428,SWALLOWING EVALUATION,\"Swallowing evaluation is a process that assesses the patient's ability to swallow safely and effectively, often involving various textures and volumes of food.\",5\r\n13675,ONCOLOGY NUTRITION FOR CLINICAL PRACTICE,A publication that provides guidelines and recommendations for nutritional support in oncology patients.,5\r\n7151,NUTRITIONAL SUPPLEMENT,\"Nutritional supplements are specialized products, such as Ensure Plus Advance and Fresubin, designed to provide essential nutrients for individuals with specific dietary needs. These supplements are particularly beneficial for patients requiring enhanced caloric and protein intake, including those managing diabetes. They serve to supp